# What `railway up` uploads as the Docker build context.
#
# Deliberately explicit rather than leaning on .gitignore. Railway also honours
# .gitignore, and in a working checkout that file excludes data/clips — which
# would hand the build an empty archive and put us straight back into the bug
# this deployment exists to avoid. Listing the exclusions here means the context
# is the same whichever tree it is run from.
#
# data/clips is NOT excluded. backend/Dockerfile bakes those 20 clips in.

.git
.gitignore
.railwayignore
.gcloudignore

# Secrets come from `railway variables`, never from a file in the image.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Rebuilt inside the container. Uploading a Windows-built venv into a Linux
# image is both slow and wrong.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The frontend deploys to Vercel, not into this image.
frontend/

# Pipeline inputs and local tooling: never executed at runtime.
data/captions/
data/*.jsonl
docs/
scripts/
.agents/
.claude/
.shots/
skills-lock.json
rushes-blueprint.md
cloudbuild.yaml
